00:03:06.110 --> 00:03:10.130
One important act today

00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:11.710
I think maybe the most important

00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:15.283
is to reassess our
vocabulary of revolution.

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:19.100
Marcello Musto has become the emcee

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:21.660
of this reassessment, the ringmaster.

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:23.110
I think I've been enormous

00:03:23.110 --> 00:03:26.350
and enormously careful
returned to Marx's texts

00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:29.640
as sources for new
understandings of vocabulary

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:31.690
we think we understand.

00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:34.760
He's gonna talk about
one of those words today.

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:36.210
I want to start each of these

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:37.910
with a quote from the author.

00:03:37.910 --> 00:03:40.800
Here's a quote from an
article on communism,

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:42.177
by Marcello Musto quote,

00:03:42.177 --> 00:03:44.377
"The alternative to capitalist alienation

00:03:44.377 --> 00:03:47.337
"was achievable only if
the sub altern classes

00:03:47.337 --> 00:03:50.507
"became aware of their
condition as new slaves

00:03:50.507 --> 00:03:51.807
"and embarked on a struggle

00:03:51.807 --> 00:03:54.277
"to radically transform the world

00:03:54.277 --> 00:03:56.597
"in which they were exploited,

00:03:56.597 --> 00:03:59.347
"their mobilization and
active participation

00:03:59.347 --> 00:04:01.687
"in this process could not stop however,

00:04:01.687 --> 00:04:04.297
"on the day after the conquest of power,

00:04:04.297 --> 00:04:06.047
"it would have to continue

00:04:06.047 --> 00:04:07.977
"in order to avert any drift towards

00:04:07.977 --> 00:04:09.477
"the kind of state socialism

00:04:09.477 --> 00:04:11.407
"that Marx's always opposed

00:04:11.407 --> 00:04:14.407
"with the utmost tenacity and conviction."

00:04:15.410 --> 00:04:18.160
A moment of Musto's pros.

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:20.070
Now I'd like to turn the microphone

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:22.690
over to my collaborator, Paul Reitter,

00:04:22.690 --> 00:04:24.620
who's a professor of German

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:28.563
at Ohio State who will intro
introduce Professor Musto.

00:04:29.630 --> 00:04:33.230
- Thanks, Paul, and
welcome Professor Musto.

00:04:33.230 --> 00:04:36.770
It's such a pleasure to
welcome you to our series.

00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:38.410
Marcela Musto is a professor

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:42.710
of sociology at York
University in Toronto.

00:04:42.710 --> 00:04:45.130
One of his most recent publications

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:47.390
is entitled "The Marx Revival"

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:52.080
and interestingly subtitled a new concepts

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:53.870
and interpretations or key concepts,

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:55.260
excuse me, and interpretations

00:04:55.260 --> 00:04:58.010
and this speaks to what
Paul was just saying

00:04:58.010 --> 00:05:01.650
about his interest in
engaging very rigorously

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:04.560
with particular categories today

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:06.273
rereading them, reassessing them.

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:11.890
And we see that in his work
on "Alienation" as well.

00:05:11.890 --> 00:05:13.250
If you've read the article

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:14.930
that was disseminated on "Alienation"

00:05:14.930 --> 00:05:17.660
you know that he writes
with tremendous erudition

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:21.010
and clarity, enviable really and

00:05:22.790 --> 00:05:24.500
to come back to this title

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:26.647
that I just mentioned "The Marx Revival,"

00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:29.360
there is a Marx revival

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:32.690
and Professor Musto is doing truly more

00:05:32.690 --> 00:05:36.300
than any other scholar I
can think of to advance it.

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:38.170
He's in addition to the qualities

00:05:38.170 --> 00:05:40.720
that I just mentioned
he's incredibly prolific.

00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:44.080
He's given over 50
interviews in recent years,

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:46.690
written over 50 newspaper articles.

00:05:46.690 --> 00:05:49.700
And also his list of publications

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:51.610
as much too long to go through

00:05:51.610 --> 00:05:53.890
in its entirety but to mention

00:05:53.890 --> 00:05:57.360
just a few things he's
edited on anthologies

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:01.220
on "Capital" 150 years later

00:06:01.220 --> 00:06:04.970
he has a massive anthology in the works on

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:08.710
or handbook really on

00:06:08.710 --> 00:06:11.510
the global dissemination of capital

00:06:12.422 --> 00:06:14.270
and the history of translations

00:06:14.270 --> 00:06:16.270
of capital around the globe.

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:20.540
He's also offered many books as well,

00:06:20.540 --> 00:06:23.350
most recently the single

00:06:23.350 --> 00:06:25.050
with many single authored books as well.

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:28.140
Most recently, "The Last
Years of Karl Marx,"

00:06:28.140 --> 00:06:31.950
which just appeared in
the spring I believe,

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:35.630
and is really a marvel of compactness.

00:06:35.630 --> 00:06:38.850
It's a biography of Marx's last years.

00:06:38.850 --> 00:06:40.130
Archivally very rich,

00:06:40.130 --> 00:06:42.380
conceptually very interesting

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:45.040
not very long either.

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:47.160
Really it's a great deal for the reader.

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:48.870
And I'd like to mention also

00:06:48.870 --> 00:06:50.750
that it was printed in Italian

00:06:50.750 --> 00:06:52.603
and came out in 2016.

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:55.390
Just to round the time

00:06:55.390 --> 00:06:57.760
that the big wave of Marx's biographies

00:06:57.760 --> 00:07:02.380
was starting to really
take shape and come at us.

00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:04.740
And it was translated very effectively.

00:07:04.740 --> 00:07:06.350
Let's not forget the translator here

00:07:06.350 --> 00:07:10.233
by Patrick Kamler into English.

00:07:11.750 --> 00:07:15.410
It's really wonderful to
have Professor Musto here.

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:17.087
The title of this presentation today is

00:07:17.087 --> 00:07:20.560
"Marx's Conception of Alienation."

00:07:20.560 --> 00:07:21.660
Thanks for being here.

00:07:23.830 --> 00:07:25.270
Thanks everybody.

