and to put together this to

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:23.460
interest for Marx like the importance

00:08:23.460 --> 00:08:25.530
of reading Marx very carefully.

00:08:25.530 --> 00:08:29.690
My work has been as
theological as possible

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:31.090
but at the same time,

00:08:31.090 --> 00:08:34.380
trying to use what Marx rightful

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:38.873
understanding our societies, our issues.

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:43.840
It is also a very strange talk for me.

00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:48.470
And I will try to make some jokes.

00:08:48.470 --> 00:08:50.870
It is the first time
in my life that I talk,

00:08:50.870 --> 00:08:53.980
not being standing like
just sitting at the table

00:08:53.980 --> 00:08:55.563
because generally I to stand.

00:08:57.740 --> 00:09:00.030
And I also used to speak

00:09:00.030 --> 00:09:04.120
as a young activist at
university in Naples.

00:09:04.120 --> 00:09:08.630
I'm Italian I was in Italy until then.

00:09:08.630 --> 00:09:13.100
I had to leave and go to
Berlin to study English.

00:09:13.100 --> 00:09:15.857
And then I moved here in Toronto in 2009.

00:09:17.045 --> 00:09:18.160
I would like to start from

