00:09:45.370 --> 00:09:48.453
and then later with more people.

00:09:49.470 --> 00:09:54.293
But when I started to speak about Marx,

00:09:56.420 --> 00:10:00.533
I have another email now, can you hear me?

00:10:08.760 --> 00:10:10.043
- We hear you find Musto.

00:10:11.590 --> 00:10:14.890
- Somebody who turn the microphone on

00:10:14.890 --> 00:10:16.720
I saw another face.

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:18.240
When I started to read Marx.

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:21.940
So when I entered my PhD in 2002 in Italy,

00:10:21.940 --> 00:10:26.480
I was actually the first researcher.

00:10:27.370 --> 00:10:29.040
The first personal was going to

00:10:29.040 --> 00:10:31.800
defend the dissertation
after so many years

00:10:31.800 --> 00:10:33.940
in such a big and important country

00:10:33.940 --> 00:10:36.230
for Marx's study like Italy.

00:10:36.230 --> 00:10:38.870
A dissertation in entirely on Marx.

00:10:38.870 --> 00:10:41.580
And later when I moved to Berlin,

00:10:41.580 --> 00:10:42.880
when I started to go there

00:10:42.880 --> 00:10:45.210
and I spent some time at the

00:10:46.350 --> 00:10:48.830
Berlin-Brandenburg
Academy, Friedrichswerder,

00:10:48.830 --> 00:10:51.550
which is the institute for social science

00:10:51.550 --> 00:10:54.310
where the new addition,

00:10:54.310 --> 00:10:55.390
the new critical additional,

00:10:55.390 --> 00:10:59.730
Marximum Engels writing
it started in 1998.

00:10:59.730 --> 00:11:01.140
That's restarted.

00:11:01.140 --> 00:11:03.100
I remember that my perception

00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:06.210
of Marx changed dramatically.

00:11:06.210 --> 00:11:07.210
And one of the points

00:11:07.210 --> 00:11:09.940
that I would like to make
today about "Capital",

00:11:09.940 --> 00:11:11.980
later we will discuss about this

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:15.110
is that after the MEGA,

00:11:15.110 --> 00:11:17.850
after this enterprise,

00:11:17.850 --> 00:11:20.453
that I was present in a minute.

00:11:21.300 --> 00:11:22.430
Looking at "Capital'

00:11:22.430 --> 00:11:24.680
like a book of three volumes,

00:11:24.680 --> 00:11:26.170
this classic set

00:11:26.170 --> 00:11:28.940
that I had seen many times in my life

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:32.860
and comparing these three volumes

00:11:32.860 --> 00:11:37.860
with 15 volumes and this
huge critical apparatus.

00:11:39.160 --> 00:11:42.433
So every volume in the
MEGA is 500, 700, 800

00:11:44.370 --> 00:11:45.530
pages of apparatus

00:11:45.530 --> 00:11:47.910
so this is the second section of the MEGA

00:11:47.910 --> 00:11:49.680
which is called "Capital"

00:11:49.680 --> 00:11:52.380
in his preparatory manuscript,

00:11:52.380 --> 00:11:53.840
is a big change.

00:11:53.840 --> 00:11:56.600
It's a big change for
us, for readers of Marx.

00:11:56.600 --> 00:12:01.160
I will go back to this point very soon

00:12:01.160 --> 00:12:03.370
for the moment I would
like to discuss with you.

00:12:03.370 --> 00:12:04.470
I would like to discuss

00:12:04.470 --> 00:12:08.150
with Professor North, Professor Reitter,

00:12:08.150 --> 00:12:09.580
Paul and Paul.

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:12.090
I would like to put a couple
of cards on the table.

00:12:12.090 --> 00:12:14.780
And the first question is what kind of

00:12:14.780 --> 00:12:16.420
revival Paul just said

00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:19.680
that there is a revival
of interest for Marx.

00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:22.110
We know this revival mostly

00:12:22.110 --> 00:12:25.270
because of what happened after 2008.

00:12:25.270 --> 00:12:30.270
After 2008, one more big
economic and financial crisis.

00:12:30.440 --> 00:12:33.610
And Marx is back in
Europe in North America,

00:12:33.610 --> 00:12:37.233
after 20 years of silence practically.

00:12:39.520 --> 00:12:41.830
So the Marx that we are reading

00:12:41.830 --> 00:12:44.970
is most of the Marx that could be

00:12:44.970 --> 00:12:46.960
the critique of political economy,

00:12:46.960 --> 00:12:48.400
the critique of capitalism

00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:52.400
and Marx was celebrated on
many important newspaper,

00:12:52.400 --> 00:12:53.720
liberal conservative.

00:12:53.720 --> 00:12:55.050
It doesn't matter.

00:12:55.050 --> 00:12:58.130
Like the person who is still useful

00:12:58.130 --> 00:13:00.280
for us not to understand capitalism

00:13:00.280 --> 00:13:04.850
including publishing
some wonderful articles

00:13:04.850 --> 00:13:08.890
that Marx wrote in 1857, 1858

00:13:08.890 --> 00:13:11.823
at the time of another
big financial crisis

00:13:11.823 --> 00:13:15.000
that started in New York 150 years

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:18.483
before the crisis they're opted in 2008.

00:13:18.483 --> 00:13:20.190
I remember I was in Berlin

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:22.490
buying the front foot that I'll get miner

00:13:22.490 --> 00:13:26.990
and being so shocked of
seeing two full pages of

00:13:26.990 --> 00:13:31.090
reprinting of the famous
article on the economic crisis

00:13:31.090 --> 00:13:34.540
that Marx wrote for the New York,

00:13:34.540 --> 00:13:37.970
New York Tribune in 1857.

00:13:37.970 --> 00:13:40.410
But in other parts of the world

00:13:40.410 --> 00:13:42.900
actually there was another reading

00:13:42.900 --> 00:13:45.610
of Marx or another interest of Marx.

00:13:45.610 --> 00:13:48.690
For example, in Latin America

00:13:48.690 --> 00:13:53.690
Marx was rediscovered a few
years before the 2008 crisis.

00:13:54.420 --> 00:13:58.780
And the return to Marx was
I would say more political

00:13:58.780 --> 00:14:00.350
than the one that we had

00:14:03.047 --> 00:14:04.800
in Europe and in North America,

00:14:04.800 --> 00:14:06.860
we got the contradictions we the problem,

00:14:06.860 --> 00:14:10.370
but it was a Marx that was alive

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:13.640
and was perceived as something useful.

00:14:13.640 --> 00:14:16.480
Now, something that people will need.

00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:21.480
And if you ask me after
this many years of work

00:14:22.040 --> 00:14:23.150
of collective work

00:14:23.150 --> 00:14:27.120
like trying to connect young researchers

00:14:27.120 --> 00:14:29.810
and institution universities

00:14:29.810 --> 00:14:33.050
and try to rediscover Marx,

00:14:33.050 --> 00:14:38.050
Paul North read this
citation at the beginning.

00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:41.770
So it's clearly a Marx
that is very different

00:14:41.770 --> 00:14:44.680
from the traditional Marxism-Leninism

00:14:44.680 --> 00:14:47.270
in the 20th century, et cetera.

00:14:47.270 --> 00:14:49.550
But if you ask me where I've seen

00:14:49.550 --> 00:14:53.180
the most interesting
things in which country

00:14:53.180 --> 00:14:55.690
I will say that Brazil is definitely

00:14:55.690 --> 00:14:57.590
the place that caught my attention

00:14:57.590 --> 00:14:59.900
more than anywhere else.

00:14:59.900 --> 00:15:03.030
I remember some people will be surprised

00:15:03.030 --> 00:15:05.450
because today Brazil is not

00:15:05.450 --> 00:15:07.360
the place where there is the most

00:15:07.360 --> 00:15:09.220
progressive government

00:15:09.220 --> 00:15:14.220
or at the moment there are not
very strong social movements

00:15:14.280 --> 00:15:17.400
like in the past couple of years,

00:15:17.400 --> 00:15:21.110
but the attention in the universities

00:15:21.110 --> 00:15:22.880
and in this research group

00:15:22.880 --> 00:15:26.550
that are not closed merrily to university,

00:15:26.550 --> 00:15:29.070
but they're open to look
at the contradiction

00:15:29.070 --> 00:15:30.580
in our societies,

00:15:30.580 --> 00:15:32.540
the attention for Marx

00:15:32.540 --> 00:15:35.340
or for an author that I also very much

00:15:35.340 --> 00:15:36.650
like Antonio Gramsci,

00:15:36.650 --> 00:15:37.840
but let's just stay too Marx

00:15:37.840 --> 00:15:40.070
so there is really impressive.

00:15:40.070 --> 00:15:42.570
I don't wanna say, give
wrong numbers, et cetera.

00:15:42.570 --> 00:15:46.530
But I think that there
are at least 150 centers

00:15:46.530 --> 00:15:48.600
of research around Marx

00:15:48.600 --> 00:15:52.250
and Marx his studies in
Brazilian universities.

00:15:52.250 --> 00:15:56.740
And when I went there to
meet some of these scholars,

00:15:56.740 --> 00:15:59.200
I was impressed by the
fact that many of them

00:15:59.200 --> 00:16:00.810
were extremely young.

00:16:00.810 --> 00:16:03.500
So they belong to a generation.

00:16:03.500 --> 00:16:06.480
It was actually younger than mine,

00:16:06.480 --> 00:16:08.770
and they had new demands

00:16:08.770 --> 00:16:11.940
that new enthusiasm and
that new new topics.

00:16:11.940 --> 00:16:14.350
And I wanna return to this
question, a new topic,

00:16:14.350 --> 00:16:18.400
because I believe that
the Marx that is read now

00:16:18.400 --> 00:16:21.240
in the last two, three years and

00:16:22.150 --> 00:16:26.357
Paul Reitter was very generous
when he described my book

00:16:26.357 --> 00:16:27.830
"The Last Years of Karl Marx."

00:16:27.830 --> 00:16:30.570
But my force in the publication

00:16:30.570 --> 00:16:34.150
of the book was trying to rediscover

00:16:34.150 --> 00:16:37.390
a Marx that is very different

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:40.190
from the perception that
we have of this author,

00:16:40.190 --> 00:16:42.220
a perception of an
author who has dedicated

00:16:42.220 --> 00:16:45.330
his entire life merrily studying

00:16:45.330 --> 00:16:48.730
or fighting politically the contradiction

00:16:48.730 --> 00:16:50.560
between capital and labor.

00:16:50.560 --> 00:16:53.600
There is much, much more in Marx.

00:16:53.600 --> 00:16:58.600
And I am very happy to
see that the majority

00:17:00.080 --> 00:17:03.060
I will say of the books
of the studies published

00:17:03.060 --> 00:17:06.540
in the last two, three
years are opening topics

00:17:06.540 --> 00:17:08.670
that neither were

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:12.170
never or very rarely associated with Marx.

00:17:12.170 --> 00:17:14.430
For example, ecology,

00:17:14.430 --> 00:17:17.570
for example, gender emancipation

00:17:17.570 --> 00:17:22.463
for example, migration,
nationalism, colonialism.

00:17:23.580 --> 00:17:25.860
I believe that there is a lot of Marx

00:17:25.860 --> 00:17:27.870
that must be discovered.

00:17:27.870 --> 00:17:31.290
And I believe that the
last part of his life,

00:17:31.290 --> 00:17:33.700
the last 10, 15 years

00:17:33.700 --> 00:17:37.740
from the international 1864, 1872

00:17:37.740 --> 00:17:41.140
to the year that Marx died in 1883,

00:17:41.140 --> 00:17:42.950
there is a lot that will be done there.

00:17:42.950 --> 00:17:45.030
And this is the task of a new generation

00:17:45.030 --> 00:17:48.100
of scholars or researchers of translators

00:17:48.100 --> 00:17:50.500
in particular of translator Paul Reitter,

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:52.650
because there is very few

00:17:52.650 --> 00:17:55.860
of Marx that has been
published in the period.

00:17:55.860 --> 00:17:58.840
And I hope that we can discuss this.

00:17:58.840 --> 00:18:00.210
I'm not lost in my talk,

00:18:00.210 --> 00:18:04.720
but I'm trying to follow what I promise.

00:18:04.720 --> 00:18:05.730
So this first

00:18:08.267 --> 00:18:09.870
group I prepared five

00:18:09.870 --> 00:18:12.190
and the first one will be a sort of

00:18:12.190 --> 00:18:14.620
the Marx survival today in the world.

00:18:14.620 --> 00:18:15.830
So I would like to say that

00:18:15.830 --> 00:18:18.610
I discovered also other kinds of revivals,

00:18:18.610 --> 00:18:20.493
for example, in China.

00:18:21.880 --> 00:18:26.800
It is impressive the amount
of books that were translated

00:18:26.800 --> 00:18:30.430
in China in the past 15, 20 years,

00:18:30.430 --> 00:18:34.140
not only there is a new very scholarly

00:18:34.140 --> 00:18:37.060
vigorous and serious additional Marx

00:18:37.060 --> 00:18:39.740
and Engels writings that
these translating also

00:18:39.740 --> 00:18:41.820
for the first time from German

00:18:41.820 --> 00:18:43.580
and not from Russian,

00:18:43.580 --> 00:18:48.150
some writings of Marx that
before at legal circulation

00:18:48.150 --> 00:18:51.210
or translation are very
ideological reading

00:18:51.210 --> 00:18:55.760
but in China that has
been also a big opening

00:18:55.760 --> 00:18:58.920
to the so called Western Marxism.

00:18:58.920 --> 00:19:03.180
Or if you don't like this
terminology too many European

00:19:03.180 --> 00:19:05.230
and North American authors.

00:19:05.230 --> 00:19:06.880
So there is a new generation

00:19:06.880 --> 00:19:09.350
of Chinese students in particular,

00:19:09.350 --> 00:19:13.020
in humanities a little
bit in social science.

00:19:13.020 --> 00:19:14.720
And I will say my experience,

00:19:14.720 --> 00:19:16.760
not at all in the economics.

00:19:16.760 --> 00:19:18.030
So I know the paradox

00:19:18.030 --> 00:19:20.560
that is repeating now also in China,

00:19:20.560 --> 00:19:24.020
that is very interested in Marx and also

00:19:24.020 --> 00:19:25.310
in this new reading.

00:19:25.310 --> 00:19:28.290
So I've always seen China

00:19:28.290 --> 00:19:31.070
as a place to compete,

00:19:31.070 --> 00:19:33.570
as a possibility to enter

00:19:33.570 --> 00:19:36.220
and also listening to

00:19:36.220 --> 00:19:38.900
what these scholars are doing are saying.

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:42.600
So I am the acquainted or over serious,

00:19:42.600 --> 00:19:43.910
that is called Marx-Engels,

00:19:43.910 --> 00:19:45.770
Marx's new dimension.

00:19:45.770 --> 00:19:49.080
And my most important at effort

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:51.880
in terms of editor is translating

00:19:51.880 --> 00:19:54.973
from Spanish, from Brazil,

00:19:56.600 --> 00:19:58.480
Portuguese, sorry, from Chinese,

00:19:58.480 --> 00:20:00.110
from Japanese countries

00:20:00.110 --> 00:20:04.200
with a very strong and lively tradition

00:20:04.200 --> 00:20:06.323
in terms of Marxist studies translate

00:20:06.323 --> 00:20:08.220
this thing into English

00:20:08.220 --> 00:20:13.220
because sometimes this
readings of Marx are different.

00:20:13.710 --> 00:20:15.850
And I find that interesting

00:20:15.850 --> 00:20:19.460
to discuss this different options

00:20:19.460 --> 00:20:21.403
these different ideas of Marx.

00:20:22.460 --> 00:20:24.427
I stop here on this point

00:20:24.427 --> 00:20:26.690
but if I ever please,

00:20:26.690 --> 00:20:27.600
two more minutes,

00:20:27.600 --> 00:20:28.980
three more minutes

00:20:28.980 --> 00:20:30.710
I will like to come back to the question

00:20:30.710 --> 00:20:35.710
of what kind of Marx is
read today at university?

00:20:35.730 --> 00:20:37.880
I spend a lot of time looking at

00:20:37.880 --> 00:20:40.440
all the syllabus around the world,

00:20:40.440 --> 00:20:42.870
and unfortunately I'm not going to

00:20:42.870 --> 00:20:44.480
share good news with you.

00:20:44.480 --> 00:20:46.530
This is at least my understanding

00:20:46.530 --> 00:20:49.090
of the situation in my opinion.

00:20:49.090 --> 00:20:51.770
I've seen that the Marx at today's read

00:20:51.770 --> 00:20:53.520
in many department of politics,

00:20:53.520 --> 00:20:56.000
political sides in the world is the Marx

00:20:56.000 --> 00:20:58.370
of on the Jewish question

00:20:58.370 --> 00:21:02.380
which is a very brilliant
actually writing.

00:21:02.380 --> 00:21:04.090
Unfortunately this writing,

00:21:04.090 --> 00:21:05.770
which is not called the Jewish question,

00:21:05.770 --> 00:21:07.470
but on the Jewish question,

00:21:07.470 --> 00:21:09.660
is reply to an article written

00:21:09.660 --> 00:21:12.080
by Bruno Bauer called "Jewish question"

00:21:12.080 --> 00:21:15.050
that was never translated into English.

00:21:15.050 --> 00:21:18.760
Well many times people do not understand

00:21:18.760 --> 00:21:20.970
what is the real polemic about.

00:21:20.970 --> 00:21:23.700
And then there is all the
party in favor of Marx.

00:21:23.700 --> 00:21:25.280
The party against Marx.

00:21:25.280 --> 00:21:26.710
Marx is doing bad things.

00:21:26.710 --> 00:21:29.087
Marx is saying all with the perfect

00:21:29.087 --> 00:21:32.570
and the right things but this text,

00:21:32.570 --> 00:21:34.570
it is surely a text

00:21:34.570 --> 00:21:36.580
that is not representative

00:21:36.580 --> 00:21:38.980
allow me to do this provocation

00:21:38.980 --> 00:21:40.770
but I'm sure that my discuss some

00:21:40.770 --> 00:21:45.080
will understand it is not
representative of Marx's politics.

00:21:45.080 --> 00:21:46.450
If you want to read Marx

00:21:46.450 --> 00:21:50.020
you have to read Marx at the
time of the international

00:21:50.020 --> 00:21:51.870
and why the text is not there

00:21:51.870 --> 00:21:54.063
because Marx at the time of international

00:21:54.063 --> 00:21:55.280
is a very complicated

00:21:55.280 --> 00:21:58.240
a complex mix of writings,

00:21:58.240 --> 00:22:01.600
documents, declarations, speeches

00:22:01.600 --> 00:22:04.770
that he did with the
exception of the civil war

00:22:04.770 --> 00:22:08.010
in France is not easy to combine

00:22:08.010 --> 00:22:11.580
and have a clear idea of Marx's positions.

00:22:11.580 --> 00:22:12.770
If you look at sociology

00:22:12.770 --> 00:22:14.680
in the department of sociology,

00:22:14.680 --> 00:22:16.320
a big majority of them

00:22:16.320 --> 00:22:18.430
they read the German ideology

00:22:18.430 --> 00:22:20.920
but today the German ideology

00:22:20.920 --> 00:22:23.183
you invited Terrell Carver last week

00:22:23.183 --> 00:22:24.647
perhaps he mentioned this,

00:22:24.647 --> 00:22:26.877
I'm not bothering you.

00:22:26.877 --> 00:22:28.270
I'm not taking time with this

00:22:28.270 --> 00:22:30.120
but today we know that the German ideology

00:22:30.120 --> 00:22:33.260
we know more than before is not a book

00:22:33.260 --> 00:22:36.370
is not the ideological Bible

00:22:36.370 --> 00:22:38.940
the four historical materialism

00:22:38.940 --> 00:22:43.120
that Soviet Union adorasky created

00:22:43.120 --> 00:22:44.440
the head of the institute

00:22:44.440 --> 00:22:48.690
for our Marx-Engels-Lenin in 1932.

00:22:48.690 --> 00:22:51.060
So if we read that the
pages on the division

00:22:51.060 --> 00:22:53.350
of labor in the German ideology,

00:22:53.350 --> 00:22:56.620
we know that this is just the beginning

00:22:56.620 --> 00:22:58.470
of a very long journey

00:22:58.470 --> 00:23:01.350
and they cannot be
compared with "Capital."

00:23:01.350 --> 00:23:02.317
But once again,

00:23:02.317 --> 00:23:05.460
"Capital" is a complicated, deep book

00:23:05.460 --> 00:23:07.750
and if you want to extract parts

00:23:07.750 --> 00:23:11.343
from there it is a difficult task.

00:23:14.860 --> 00:23:17.923
- [Paul] Can I ask you
a couple of questions?

00:23:19.560 --> 00:23:21.520
It looks like he is spotlighted

00:23:21.520 --> 00:23:22.840
and I'm not showing up.

00:23:22.840 --> 00:23:26.523
I'm not sure this is a problem.

00:23:27.860 --> 00:23:28.760
Cause we wanna make sure that

00:23:28.760 --> 00:23:31.620
the people who ask questions..

00:23:31.620 --> 00:23:34.083
Or do you all see me when I'm speaking?

00:23:34.083 --> 00:23:35.430
- I do.
- Yeah.

00:23:35.430 --> 00:23:37.140
I just don't see myself.

00:23:37.140 --> 00:23:38.610
I want it to, well, first I wanted

00:23:38.610 --> 00:23:41.300
to thank you for the picture of a kind

00:23:41.300 --> 00:23:44.700
of textual international,

00:23:44.700 --> 00:23:46.790
which we hope proceeds the fifth

00:23:46.790 --> 00:23:48.820
or whatever international is coming

00:23:48.820 --> 00:23:50.360
a political international.

00:23:50.360 --> 00:23:51.470
It really is encouraging

00:23:51.470 --> 00:23:53.720
for people who read these things

00:23:53.720 --> 00:23:56.230
to know how much is going on.

00:23:56.230 --> 00:24:01.230
Also for the picture of a
reconfiguration of the Corpus,

00:24:01.690 --> 00:24:03.680
which is an interesting phenomenon.

00:24:03.680 --> 00:24:05.550
And I think we all need to say

00:24:05.550 --> 00:24:08.210
where to start reading Marx

00:24:08.210 --> 00:24:09.810
where to go next.

00:24:09.810 --> 00:24:14.810
What for what pitfalls to ignore.

00:24:14.970 --> 00:24:16.170
I wanted to ask you though,

00:24:16.170 --> 00:24:19.680
in this world flowering of Marx studies

00:24:19.680 --> 00:24:21.903
and in the reconfiguration of the Corpus,

00:24:24.080 --> 00:24:28.360
what role does alienation play in that?

00:24:28.360 --> 00:24:30.640
You're gonna talk about alienation today.

00:24:30.640 --> 00:24:33.210
Is it a hot button issue?

00:24:33.210 --> 00:24:35.453
Is everyone worried about alienation?

00:24:36.810 --> 00:24:38.933
Where should it fit in the new program?

00:24:40.130 --> 00:24:43.900
- Thanks. And when I talk too much,

00:24:43.900 --> 00:24:46.430
like when I pass the 12 minutes

00:24:46.430 --> 00:24:49.450
and more or less we are
located for each block,

00:24:49.450 --> 00:24:52.720
I will be very grateful
if you or Paul Reitter

00:24:52.720 --> 00:24:55.110
you just stopped me

00:24:55.110 --> 00:24:56.580
very politely as you did,

00:24:56.580 --> 00:24:59.410
but you helped me to move forward.

00:24:59.410 --> 00:25:02.060
Surprisingly I want to discuss,

00:25:02.060 --> 00:25:04.700
I want to answer briefly shortly

00:25:04.700 --> 00:25:06.470
and then I will expand this.

00:25:06.470 --> 00:25:10.370
Surprisingly, even though alienation

00:25:10.370 --> 00:25:13.210
is a topic on which there were

00:25:13.210 --> 00:25:16.180
so many books written in the sixties

00:25:16.180 --> 00:25:21.037
in the seventies and
alienation was I would say,

00:25:23.200 --> 00:25:25.760
as relevant as the topic globalization

00:25:25.760 --> 00:25:29.600
has been for us in the past two decades.

00:25:29.600 --> 00:25:32.530
Really everybody wrote about alienation

00:25:32.530 --> 00:25:36.000
and I can think in the sixties

00:25:36.000 --> 00:25:37.270
and in the seventies,

00:25:37.270 --> 00:25:40.170
in many disciplines in sociology,

00:25:40.170 --> 00:25:43.930
in politics, in psychology, literature

00:25:45.800 --> 00:25:49.520
few terms at the fortune of alienation

00:25:49.520 --> 00:25:53.510
and Marx alienation not
conception of alienation,

00:25:53.510 --> 00:25:55.380
which is the title of my talk.

00:25:55.380 --> 00:25:58.950
My contribution today
was the most important

00:26:00.300 --> 00:26:03.440
element of analysis.

00:26:03.440 --> 00:26:08.130
Despite this, when you
publish on alienation today

00:26:08.130 --> 00:26:09.650
and when you put actually

00:26:09.650 --> 00:26:11.540
the word alienation in the title,

00:26:11.540 --> 00:26:15.570
I notice that there is
an incredible interest,

00:26:15.570 --> 00:26:17.810
even more than usual.

00:26:17.810 --> 00:26:21.520
And there are many books

00:26:21.520 --> 00:26:25.970
many articles published on
alienation or on fetishism.

00:26:25.970 --> 00:26:30.800
So in this rediscovery of
Marx in this "Marx's Revival"

00:26:30.800 --> 00:26:33.780
I see that there is a lot about alienation

00:26:33.780 --> 00:26:35.310
and about fetishism.

00:26:35.310 --> 00:26:37.330
And let's try to discuss together.

00:26:37.330 --> 00:26:38.163
Please help me.

00:26:38.163 --> 00:26:38.996
I need your help.

00:26:39.880 --> 00:26:41.583
Why this is possible?

00:26:43.160 --> 00:26:45.280
I have an answer.

00:26:45.280 --> 00:26:50.280
I will try to provide my idea, my opinion

00:26:51.330 --> 00:26:53.800
and then we'll see what you two believe.

00:26:53.800 --> 00:26:56.590
And then there will be question criticism.

00:26:56.590 --> 00:27:01.590
So even though alienation
for us is a classic

00:27:01.780 --> 00:27:03.250
in the Marxist thoughts.

00:27:03.250 --> 00:27:06.660
And if we look at the topics alienation

00:27:06.660 --> 00:27:09.610
is perhaps one of the top five topics

00:27:09.610 --> 00:27:11.997
like Marx's alienation is as important

00:27:11.997 --> 00:27:13.810
and Marx and communism

00:27:13.810 --> 00:27:16.630
and Marx and critical political economy.

00:27:16.630 --> 00:27:18.760
I want to say that this phenomenon

00:27:18.760 --> 00:27:21.670
is something very, very recent.

00:27:21.670 --> 00:27:25.670
And here I'm talking to the
students who are listening.

00:27:25.670 --> 00:27:27.980
I will be a little bit boring

00:27:27.980 --> 00:27:30.243
for those who are big Marx experts.

00:27:32.414 --> 00:27:34.880
But I would like to spend a couple

00:27:34.880 --> 00:27:36.990
of minutes discussing this with students.

00:27:36.990 --> 00:27:39.330
I lost Paul North for the moment,

00:27:39.330 --> 00:27:41.970
but he's back now.

00:27:41.970 --> 00:27:44.653
So why alienation is something new?

00:27:45.520 --> 00:27:49.960
Alienation something because the text,

00:27:49.960 --> 00:27:51.420
which is not a book

00:27:51.420 --> 00:27:55.593
but it's a very, very
first stage manuscript

00:27:55.593 --> 00:27:57.960
