01:11:01.330 --> 01:11:04.800
that Marx brought between 62 and 63.

01:11:04.800 --> 01:11:05.830
There is a lot.

01:11:05.830 --> 01:11:10.260
So I learn a lot when I read this texts.

01:11:10.260 --> 01:11:12.480
I understand alienation

01:11:12.480 --> 01:11:14.350
but actually more than
understanding alienation,

01:11:14.350 --> 01:11:16.820
I understand capitalism much better

01:11:16.820 --> 01:11:20.180
than when I read the texts of 1844.

01:11:20.180 --> 01:11:23.977
And then the final part here, "Capital."

01:11:25.020 --> 01:11:27.690
This really when Marx
is writing "Capital."

01:11:27.690 --> 01:11:30.950
So these are not manuscript
written for himself.

01:11:30.950 --> 01:11:33.800
This is a very important for us.

01:11:33.800 --> 01:11:36.650
The so called "Unpublished Chapter VI."

01:11:36.650 --> 01:11:38.960
Marx's returning on this question

01:11:38.960 --> 01:11:41.430
with very brilliant, beautiful way.

01:11:41.430 --> 01:11:42.970
These are all the places where

01:11:42.970 --> 01:11:46.860
you find the ideas that
"Capital" is bombarded.

01:11:46.860 --> 01:11:50.330
Mistaking the blood of
leaving labor, et cetera.

01:11:50.330 --> 01:11:52.700
And then this is what
Paul Reitter mentioned

01:11:52.700 --> 01:11:57.700
at the beginning, the
famous section of volume one

01:11:58.007 --> 01:12:01.700
and there is also chapter
"Capital, Volume III."

01:12:01.700 --> 01:12:03.980
Okay. So there is a lot of "Capital"

01:12:03.980 --> 01:12:08.980
that is a lot of alienation that you find.

01:12:09.540 --> 01:12:11.570
And the part that you find

01:12:11.570 --> 01:12:14.560
in the early writings
is a very minoritarian

01:12:15.630 --> 01:12:18.723
and perhaps not even
the most important one.

01:12:20.900 --> 01:12:22.000
